       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-03 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cultural Activists Protest Delay in Tagore Centenary Hall Reconstruction</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Cultural activists in Kozhikode staged a protest at the Corporation office demanding the urgent reconstruction of the demolished Tagore Centenary Hall. The former 1,200-seat venue was torn down years ago due to structural issues, leaving local artists without an affordable, large-capacity space for performances.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/cultural-activists-protest-delay-in-tagore-centenary-hall-re.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Protesters criticized the lack of alternative arrangements, noting that existing venues are either too small or prohibitively expensive. While the Corporation cited previous funding setbacks and is currently seeking Central grants for the project, activists urged officials to expedite the process to restore access to cultural infrastructure in the city.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the protest and the context regarding the Tagore Centenary Hall reconstruction.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/a-song-or-two-for-the-reconstruction-of-tagore-centenary-hall-in-kozhikode/article71661308.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
