     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Civic Body Proposes Doubling Parking Fees Under GRAP II</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Municipal Corporation of Delhi (MCD) plans to double parking charges at approximately 400 surface lots to combat worsening air quality under GRAP II restrictions. The proposal, awaiting final approval, would increase standard rates from the current Rs 20 for four-wheelers and Rs 10 for two-wheelers.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/delhi-civic-body-proposes-doubling-parking-fees-under-grap-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Implementation faces hurdles regarding existing contracts with private operators, as current agreements lack provisions for the MCD to retain additional revenue generated by rate hikes. Contractors may also seek compensation if vehicle traffic declines due to pollution-related restrictions. The New Delhi Municipal Council has already implemented similar fee increases as of November 1.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the MCD proposal and the associated contractual obstacles.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/delhi-mcd-parking-charges-double-400-lots-grap-ii-pollution-curbs-ptag-3031686-2026-11-03?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
