     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-11-03 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Navy rescues hijacked fishing vessel off Somalia</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Navy</span> <span>#Maritime Security</span> <span>#Somalia</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Navy has successfully rescued a hijacked fishing vessel operating off the coast of Somalia. According to the DD News summary, the operation resulted in the safe release of all 20 crew members who had been held captive on the ship.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/indian-navy-rescues-hijacked-fishing-vessel-off-somalia.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This mission highlights the ongoing efforts of the Indian Navy to combat maritime piracy in the region. No further details regarding the specific identity of the vessel or the timeline of the hijacking were provided in the summary. The rescue operation confirms the commitment of the agency to maritime security and the protection of international shipping lanes against illegal activities.</p><p>What to watch: Further official reports regarding the identity of the pirates involved in the hijacking.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the brief source provided, though limited by the brevity of the source material itself.</p>
