     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-03 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Universities Decline in QS Asia Rankings; IITs, IISc Out of Top 50 for Second Year</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#QS Asia Rankings</span> <span>#Indian Universities</span> <span>#IITs</span> <span>#IISc</span></div>
       <p>Indian universities have experienced a further decline in the latest QS Asia rankings, according to a report by ThePrint. This downturn reflects a broader challenge for higher education institutions in the country.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/indian-universities-decline-in-qs-asia-rankings-iits-iisc-ou.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Notably, none of the Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs) or the Indian Institute of Science (IISc) managed to secure a spot within the top 50 in these prestigious regional rankings. This marks the second consecutive year that these prominent institutions have been absent from the top 50 cohort.</p><p>The consistent absence of leading Indian institutions from the top 50 positions in the QS Asia rankings for two years running underscores ongoing performance issues within the higher education sector.</p><p>What to watch: Future strategies for improving global university standings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft covers the core facts from the source summary effectively and maintains a clear, news-oriented structure.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
