       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>New Book on Experiential Learning Released by TGCHE Chairman</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana IT Minister Duddilla Sridhar Babu officially released the book 'Experiential Learning: A Game Changer in Higher Education' on November 2, 2026. Authored by V. Balakista Reddy, Chairman of the Telangana Council of Higher Education, the text advocates for an application-oriented curriculum that prioritizes internships, hands-on projects, and industry interactions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/new-book-on-experiential-learning-released-by-tgche-chairman.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The book is designed for both undergraduate and postgraduate students to bridge the gap between classroom theory and real-world practice. Mr. Reddy stated that the TGCHE is prioritizing academic reforms to ensure graduates are industry-ready by integrating practical skills with traditional academic knowledge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the book release and the stated objectives of the TGCHE Chairman.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/tgche-chairmans-book-on-experiential-learning-released/article71656717.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
