       <h1>Rajkumari Lanchenbi Chanu Secures India's First Wushu Medal at Youth Olympic Games</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Wushu</span> <span>#Youth Olympic Games</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Rajkumari Lanchenbi Chanu made history on Tuesday by becoming the first Indian athlete to win a wushu medal at the Youth Olympic Games. She clinched a bronze medal in the women's Changquan combined event, marking a significant milestone for India in the sport.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/rajkumari-lanchenbi-chanu-secures-indias-first-wushu-medal-a.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Her achievement represents a breakthrough for Indian wushu on the international youth stage. The bronze medal in the Changquan combined event highlights her skill and dedication in this martial art discipline.</p><p>This historic win positions Rajkumari Lanchenbi Chanu as a pioneer for future Indian wushu athletes aspiring to compete at the Youth Olympic Games. Her performance is expected to inspire greater participation and recognition for wushu in India.</p><p>What to watch: Future performances of Indian wushu athletes in international competitions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise, accurate, and captures all the essential information provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/othersports/rajkumari-lanchenbi-chanu-wins-indias-first-ever-medal-in-wushu-at-youth-olympic-games-12278424#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
