       <h1>Reggie Releases Diss Track Against Kai Cenat Before Court Appearance</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Streamer Reggie released a diss track titled &quot;Before Court&quot; on November 3, 2026, hours before a scheduled court hearing regarding a protective order filed by Kai Cenat. The song features lyrics questioning Cenat's toughness, escalating their ongoing dispute that began in September when Reggie left the Clover Boys group.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/reggie-releases-diss-track-against-kai-cenat-before-court-ap.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Cenat previously issued a cease-and-desist letter on October 2, alleging Reggie made false claims and threats. While the court's decision on the protective order remains pending, the release of the track signals Reggie's intent to continue the public confrontation despite the legal proceedings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise, highly dense, and captures all key details accurately without padding.</p>
