     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-03 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tendulkar Cautions Against Early Leadership for Teenage Sensation Sooryavanshi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#Vaibhav Sooryavanshi</span> <span>#Sachin Tendulkar</span> <span>#Duleep Trophy</span></div>
       <p>India's teenage cricketing sensation, Vaibhav Sooryavanshi, has become the nation's youngest international cricketer at 15 years and 99 days, surpassing Sachin Tendulkar's previous record of 16 years and 205 days at Test debut. Sooryavanshi's rapid ascent through the ranks, including his recent appointment as vice-captain of East Zone for the 2026-27 Duleep Trophy, has prompted a candid reflection from the cricket legend, Sachin Tendulkar, regarding the pace of the young batter's progression.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/tendulkar-cautions-against-early-leadership-for-teenage-sens.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During a recent Reddit Q&amp;A session, Tendulkar shared his concerns about Sooryavanshi being handed captaincy responsibilities at such a young age. He advised a measured path, emphasizing the importance of gradual development over rapid advancement. &quot;I feel it's too early for him to become a vice-captain in the Duleep Trophy. We have to let him play more matches with the red ball and take one step at a time!&quot; Tendulkar wrote, advocating for more red-ball exposure for the promising talent.</p><p>Sooryavanshi's exceptional talent is evident across multiple formats. In the 2025-26 Vijay Hazare Trophy, he made history by striking a 36-ball century against Arunachal Pradesh, becoming the youngest player to score a List A hundred at 14 years and 272 days. His performances in the Indian Premier League have also cemented his status as a top scorer in the competition. However, Tendulkar's counsel stresses that long-term development, particularly in red-ball cricket, should precede leadership roles.</p><p>This philosophy aligns with the approach articulated by India's head coach, Gautam Gambhir, who emphasizes backing consistent performers. Gambhir previously stated, &quot;Guys who have done phenomenally well over a longer period of time obviously deserve a longer rope.&quot; The value of experience and consistency at the international level was also demonstrated in India's T20I World Cup triumph in 2026, where top-order batters Sanju Samson and Abhishek Sharma played key roles. Tendulkar's advice underscores the importance of a solid foundation for young players before their elevation to significant leadership positions.</p><p>What to watch: Sooryavanshi's continued development in red-ball cricket and future leadership progression.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the source material, providing context on Tendulkar's comments and the broader philosophy regarding young player development.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/sachin-tendulkar-urges-caution-as-vaibhav-sooryavanshis-teenage-stardom-accelerates/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
