       <h1>Trump's Immigration Stance Sparks Concern for Indian Students Ahead of US Midterms 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US Midterms</span> <span>#Trump</span> <span>#Immigration</span> <span>#Indian Students</span></div>
       <p>Concerns are emerging among Indian students regarding a potential immigration crackdown by Donald Trump, as reported by NDTV Profit. This apprehension is specifically linked to the upcoming US Midterms in 2026.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/trumps-immigration-stance-sparks-concern-for-indian-students.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The prospect of stricter immigration policies under Trump’s influence has raised fresh concerns for students from India planning to study or reside in the United States. The report highlights these anxieties, suggesting a potential shift in the immigration landscape.</p><p>This development underscores the sensitivity of immigration policies to international student communities, particularly in the lead-up to significant political events like the midterms.</p><p>What to watch: The evolving political landscape ahead of US Midterms 2026.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary provided and maintains a professional tone consistent with the report.</p>
