     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-03 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>US Midterm Elections 2026: Seven Key Battlegrounds Determine Congressional Control</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 2026 US midterm elections serve as a critical referendum on President Donald Trump’s second-term agenda, with control of Congress at stake. Democrats are targeting narrow-margin races to potentially constrain Trump’s legislative power and increase oversight, while Republicans defend their majorities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-03/us-midterm-elections-2026-seven-key-battlegrounds-determine-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Seven states have emerged as pivotal battlegrounds. Notable contests include Texas, where Democrats challenge Republican strongholds for Senate and gubernatorial seats; Ohio, featuring a comeback bid by former Senator Sherrod Brown; and Michigan, where a contentious Senate race for Gary Peters’ seat could decide control of the upper chamber. These high-stakes elections will significantly reshape the American political landscape ahead of the 2028 presidential cycle.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the high-stakes nature of the midterms and identifies the battleground states as requested.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
